Maybe the moral of the story is to use vi-controls rather than 
numpad...  Oh yes, I went there!  IMHO, it's overwhelmingly worth the 
short learning curve to be able to play with both hands on the 
homerow.

On the other hand (NPI), one problem I have involving "stupid fingers" 
is getting in a hurry in minetown or similar and trying to go left 
into a guard, then immediately hitting "y" for diagonally up-and-left 
just out of a reflex to avoid the occupied square, thereby answering 
"yes" to "do you really want to attack?", angering the guard and 
leading to a mad dash for my life and/or the staircase.  So maybe 
that's one reason why not to use hjkl control...  Personally, I'd like 
to see the affirmative response to these types of questions be a 
capital "Y" rather than the lower case "y".



